{"step_index":17,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:50:13Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Walkthrough and user guide for the Smart City Logistics Carpooling System C++ DSA Visualizer","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Smart City Logistics – Carpooling System (C++ DSA Live Visualizer)\n\nA modern, interactive Web Application designed with a dark-mode cyberpunk glassmorphism aesthetic, dynamic mouse-driven 3D anti-gravity tilt physics, and real-time visualization of C++ backend Data Structures & Algorithms.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Live Files & Direct Access\n- **Application Page**: [index.html](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html)\n- **Styling & 3D CSS Physics**: [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/styles.css)\n- **C++ Engine & 3D Canvas Logic**: [app.js](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/app.js)\n\n---\n\n## 🎮 Interactive Features & Modules Walkthrough\n\n### 1. 3D Spatial City Graph & Dijkstra Shortest Path\n- **Data Structures**: Graph (Adjacency List with edge weights) + Min-Heap Priority Queue (`std::priority_queue<Pair, vector<Pair>, greater<Pair>>`).\n- **Interactive Orbit**: Click and drag on the 3D City Map to rotate the city grid in true 3D spatial perspective; scroll to zoom in/out.\n- **Dijkstra Calculation**: Choose any Source and Destination hub, click **\"Compute Shortest Path\"**, and watch the neon laser path illuminate along with step-by-step Min-Heap relaxation trace pills.\n\n### 2. Dual Passenger Queues (FIFO Pipeline & 3D Circular Ring Buffer)\n- **Dynamic FIFO Queue**: Add passengers through the input bar to observe the dynamic pipeline showing `FRONT (HEAD)` to `REAR`.\n- **3D Circular Buffer (Fixed Array Size 5)**: Push unmatched or standby passengers to watch circular index pointers `F: [front] | R: [rear]` update modulo 5 (`(front + count) % 5`) with overflow/underflow safeguards.\n\n### 3. Driver Registry & Hash Table with Chaining\n- **Singly Linked List**: New drivers are dynamically prepended/appended with `Driver* head` and `next` pointer visualization cards.\n- **Hash Table with Chaining**: Maps Driver IDs to buckets using `hash(DriverID) % 6`. Enter an ID in the query box to trigger an $O(1)$ search and bucket highlighting.\n\n### 4. Active Confirmed Rides & BST Registry\n- **Doubly Linked List**: Matches front passengers with available drivers, decrementing available seats and displaying active trips with bidirectional `prev <-> next` link cards and cancellation hooks.\n- **Binary Search Tree (BST)**: Every confirmed ride is inserted into an interactive BST sorted by Ride ID, complete with automatic node branching, glowing canvas rendering, and live in-order traversal readouts.\n\n### 5. Ride Undo Mechanism (LIFO Stack)\n- Backed by an undo history stack (`std::stack<UndoAction>`).\n- Clicking **\"Undo Latest Ride (Stack Pop)\"** immediately pops the topmost ride frame, frees the trip, restores the driver's available seat count, and puts the passenger back at the front of the queue.\n\n### 6. C++ Backend Code Inspection Drawer\n- Click **\"C++ Backend Structs\"** in the top navigation bar to open a syntax-highlighted code drawer showing the exact native C++ structs (`struct DriverNode`, `struct ActiveRideNode`, `dijkstra()`, `CircularWaitlistQueue`, `RideBST`, `RideUndoManager`) mirroring each UI action.\n","Description":"Created walkthrough.md documenting all modules, physics effects, and data structures.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Kartik Bhosle\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Writing walkthrough file","toolSummary":"Create walkthrough.md in artifacts directory"}}]}
